    "turn_text": "that we can do that don't actually require Congress. I've partnered, for example, with Representative Clyburn to be creating partnerships with technology companies at HBCUs, Benedict College, Cloughlin, but not just there, but at HSIs and rural communities. So how do we convene business and technology leaders to create new jobs, new economic opportunity? We've been pushing what the president calls Bidenomics, which put simply is We got to make more things in America. That's not a partisan issue. I mean, I was in Johnstown, Pennsylvania recently, Bakari, and totally decimated town in Pennsylvania. I was shocked to learn that the top 15 steel plants in the world are now not in America. The majority are in China and other parts. We don't have a single one in the top 15. How did we let that happen? How do we bring manufacturing back? So those are, I think, two of my focuses, two of the Congress and presidents' focuses.",
