  {
    "episode_id": 76281,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76281.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm a supporter of Barbara Lee in that race. She's been a friend. She's a neighbor. A colleague, I've admired her since she cast the lone vote against a prolonged war in Afghanistan. I thought she'd be great. And when she decided to get in, I said, we're not going to have two progressives. And I'm happy to defer to her. And I also feel like the game has changed. It used to be you had to go to the Senate. or the governorship before a state of the union would even know of your existence. Now you've got people like Jamie Raskin deciding not to run for the Senate, and the House is actually a very happening place with a lot of the next generation leaders there. It's going to be a challenging race. Barbara knows she's the underdog, and Adam Schiff is very formidable. I think he raised $8 million or",
